 directly from the SAP Cloud Transport Management user interface. Like this, you can obtain the MTA logs without using the Cloud Foundry command- line interface (cf cli).   See:   Options to Display Information about Transport Requests  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413b\n\n--- Record 1555 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Option to download transport action logs in a .csv file format.\nDescription: You can now download transport action logs as .csv files, either individually or all at once. This structured format simplifies data analysis and enhances audit compliance.  See:   Transport Action Logs  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413b\n\n--- Record 1556 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Destination Service - New Features\nDescription:   When calling the Destination service, you can now provide a previously generated and signed SAML assertion when fetching an OAuth2SAMLBearerAssertion destination. This SAML assertion will be exchanged for a token with the configured token service, instead of the Destination service generating one based on a provided user token.  A new Destinations UI for managing destination configuration objects is now available as a BETA version in the SAP BTP cockpit, side-by-side with the current UI. It is not yet at feature parity with the current UI, but feel free to try it out and send us your feedback.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1557 ---\nComponent: Extensions\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma